      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this happening ? It sounds to me from your comment that the control comes here when keepalive was started and encountered an error, in which case the state goes to NOT_STARTED but the slot is not free yet, so when the stop() command comes we go to STOPPING.\n\nIf my understanding is accurate, then this is not the right solution. The right solution would involve going to STOPPING when the error occurs. In particular, if an error causes the state to go to NOT_STARTED but not release the slot, then it\u0027s still possible for a START command to come in the mean time and the issue is not fixed.",
      "range": {
